module gunbc.rung_drop.floor_cut_falsifier_cadence

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing }

data floor_cut_falsifier_cadence: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "floor_cut_falsifier_cadence" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "Falsifier cadence: exposure open, disposition NOT decided",

  declared: "2026-09-01",

  standing: Standing,

  authored: "**THE FALSIFIER CADENCE IS GONE AND WHETHER IT SHOULD RETURN IS AN OPEN OPERATOR QUESTION, WHICH IS WHY THIS ROW IS NEITHER A RESTORATION NOR A RETIREMENT (2026-09-01).** Split out of `floor_cut`. PREVIOUS RUNG: 2 (mechanically preventable) -- a scheduled cadence ran a predict-only cold comparison over the whole corpus, so a wrong affected-set prediction and a lying `SubstrateInputsOnly` disposition surfaced as a counted divergence within one window. TEMPORARY RUNG: 0 -- `falsifier.yml` was deleted by the cut and the repository carries three workflows, none of which runs a cold comparison. `v2.std.live_tree` records the consequence in its own words: two carriers named that cadence as their enforcement, the sentences were true when written and became false when the workflow died, and nothing could notice. BOUNDED POPULATION: one capability -- a scheduled whole-corpus cold control against the selected run. WHY THE DISPOSITION IS OPEN AND STATED AS OPEN. `docs/plans/floor-cut-replacement-plan.md` item 8 says `proposed: never returns`. That is a PROPOSAL in a hand-authored plan, not a ruling, and a capability deliberately not returning is a SCOPE REMOVAL, which is the operator's call and not an author's. Writing this row as a restoration that will wait forever would be a trigger that cannot fire; writing it as retired would be an author retiring an operator's exposure. RESTORATION TRIGGER, TWO ARMS AND NO OTHERS: this row retires EITHER when a scheduled consumer executes a predict-only cold comparison over the whole corpus and reports divergences as a counted, located population, OR when an OPERATOR RULES the capability withdrawn -- at which point the row is retired citing that ruling, and the carriers that named the cadence as their enforcement must be corrected in the same change, because a withdrawn capability still leaves them asserting a route that does not exist. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE THIS ROW: an author, a lane or a plan concluding it should never return. **`floor_cut` CANNOT RETIRE WHILE THIS ROW STANDS**, and this sentence is on every one of the five so the constraint is readable from either end: that row's trigger is the conjunction of these five, so retiring it on a reading of any single sibling -- including this one -- is the reading its own trigger forbids."
}
